OL,3,GNEWSACommunity rallies around after
OL,4,Apaint thrown at pub
OL,5,
OL,6,FA landlady has thanked neighbours for
OL,7,Ftheir support after paint was thrown
OL,8,Fover her and her husband's pub.
OL,10,FAleks Earl said she and her husband
OL,11,FNoah had it had been "absolutely
OL,12,Fheartbreaking" to find their pub, the
OL,13,FShip Inn in Mevagissey, had been
OL,14,Fcovered in white paint.
OL,16,FShe said it had been "devastating" to
OL,17,Fsee the damage on Wednesday but
OL,18,Fvillagers had sprung into action to
OL,19,Fclean the paint up and in doing so had
OL,20,F"reminded us exactly why we love being
OL,21,Fpart of Mevagissey".
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
